From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeeJayBaker <Tom_John_baker@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:09:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Overcooked! All You Can Eat: profile (update 1.0.11, Unity
 2019.4.11f1)

From the NSP script's provisional profile, with the update's real version (v720896) and the new
Unity keys: unity_tier 2, unity_skip_keywords (lightmap and cookie keywords no scene, renderer or
light enables) and unity_skip_passes META cut the split from 520,394 to 45,221 shaders, a 198 MB
package and 28,928 pipeline pairs. Plays on the Mac: a 35-minute run at 30 fps on an M1 Pro took in
the menus, two DLC world maps and a level on each, with no shader missing from the map. iOS is
untested.

depth_mode zero: the game selects near-zero NVN depth, so the pipeline archive made offline uses
the main0_z vertex entry. Without it the bundled archive was rejected and the first boot built
34,444 pipeline pairs itself (227 s).

present_interval display: the game asks for present interval 2 and holds nothing else at 30, so it
runs at 60 fps (59.9-60.0 over 16,200 frames on the M1 Pro, from an app built with this profile,
whose 305 pipeline bases all came from the archive, 1.5 s before the first frame).

README gallery: a Mac screenshot, noted 60 fps with 1.0.11.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#836
Reason: Overcooked! All You Can Eat has no upstream profile yet
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#369

