+# Game profile of Overcooked! All You Can Eat (Switch, update 1.0.11 = v720896)
+# Format: see dm/games/README.md
+# Unity 2019.4.11f1 (IL2CPP) with FMOD and Pia, SDK 10.4.1. Brought up from the NSP script's provisional profile: the memory values are its measured guesses.
+# The shaders are Unity's Shader objects in the Addressables bundles in StreamingAssets/aa/Switch, read by unityfs.py with Unity 2019.4's layouts
+
+# ---- Identity ----
+title_id	0100F28011892000
+program_id	0100F28011892000
+
+# ---- App ----
+# Game name: only a label for profile listings and the Mac window title; the iOS app name is the game name in the base NSP, and the bundle ID comes from the base game title ID (build_ipa.sh / NSP script)
+name	Overcooked! All You Can Eat
+ipa	OvercookedAllYouCanEat.ipa
+app_category	public.app-category.games
+
+# ---- Versions ----
+build	v720896	1.0.11	main=2854968f71a67b45a98014d9b6fae180	subsdk0=84e50460493a12f26100e5150fbff271	sdk=d9add76fc264863d85fbbd1d70076c76
+package	v720896
+shader_versions	v720896
+
+# ---- Files ----
+# load order as on Horizon: main, subsdk*, sdk (subsdk0 = NintendoSDK_movie)
+modules	main subsdk0 sdk
+romfs_marker	Data/StreamingAssets/aa/Switch/Switch/chefs_assets_all.bundle
+zip_store	.assets:.bundle:.dat:.json:.png:.resource:.ress:.metallib
+
+# ---- Memory ----
+# The NPDM declares 16 MB of system resource, so IsVirtualAddressMemoryEnabled is true. The 5 GB block with a 4.375 GB alias region: in its first 15 s the game's
+# regions reach alias +3.38 GB (the NSP script's address region check, 2026-10-31); the heap check found no heap set
+sys_resource	0x1000000
+mem_reserve	0x140000000
+mem_alias	0x118000000
+mem_stack	0x10000000
+app_pool	0xCD500000
+
+# ---- Frame rate ----
+# The game asks for present interval 2 (30 fps on the Switch) and holds nothing else at 30: one frame per display tick gives 60 fps on the Mac (README.md, Frame rate).
+# DM_PRESENT_INTERVAL=game keeps 30 and saves power
+present_interval	display
+
+# ---- Shader split ----
+# The registered build selects near-zero NVN depth; offline pipeline bases use main0_z.
+depth_mode	zero
+shader_groups	/Data/=data
+shader_note	Overcooked! All You Can Eat shaders
+# The player runs hardware tier 2 (Unity's Tier3); what each key leaves out and why: README.md, Shaders
+unity_tier	2
+unity_skip_keywords	DIRLIGHTMAP_SEPARATE DIRLIGHTMAP_COMBINED DYNAMICLIGHTMAP_ON POINT_COOKIE DIRECTIONAL_COOKIE
+unity_skip_passes	META
